  "gameData": {
    "backstory": "Found as a hatchling abandoned in the toxic mud flats outside Subchain City, 'Tongue-Tied' Terry was raised by a pack of feral bots who taught him the value of scavenging and a healthy distrust of everyone. He earned his nickname honestly, by accidentally ingesting a particularly potent strain of mutated algae that permanently extended his tongue, much to the amusement (and disgust) of his bot-kin.",
    "class": "Mad-Max Medic",
    "name": "Tongue-Tied Terry",
    "personality": "Cynical and resourceful, Terry is a font of dark humor and grim pragmatism. Though he acts like he doesn't care, he secretly harbors a soft spot for the underdog (or under-duck) and will begrudgingly lend a helping glove to those in need… for a price.",
    "specialAbility": {
      "description": "Terry can use his abnormally long tongue to whip enemies, dealing ranged damage and potentially inflicting the 'Slimed' condition, reducing their agility for 2 turns.  His Featherguard Shadow armor grants him a defensive buff after using this ability.",
